      "id": 38806,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-18T21:45:44.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I think it's in the wording and timing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If he uses the Rod's power first, he can still use Strike \"twice this turn\" and can thus use it twice. (It doesn't say one additional time - it says twice.  :grin: )</li>\n<li>If he uses Strike first, he's used his power, so he can't use the Rod's power but he can use Strike a second time.</li>\n</ul>\n \n<p>Just my opinion, though - not an official answer.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"></p>",
      "post_number": 3,
